# Future data tooling

`build.py` writes train/dev-only separated bundles from an explicit pinned plan.
`seal.py` is the separately authorized custodian-only future host entrypoint and
refuses a standalone mutation without an injected trusted receipt verifier and
matching frozen lifecycle. `custody.py` provides value-free inventory/bundle/store
inspection and source-pin summaries. None has been executed in Dirty Mode. They use only local source/files and do
not install, download or call models. The shipped development inventory is not a
held-out corpus. Read `docs/data-custody.md` before using any command.
